\mt2 The first letter from
\mt1 Simon ‘the Rock’ (Peter)
\is1 Introduction
\ip \bk The second letter from Simon ‘the rock Peter’\bk* was sent to believers in various towns of Asia Minor (also called Anatolia, now part of modern Turkey) (1 Peter 1:1, 2 Peter 3:1). His purpose of writing this was to contradict the work of false teachers, and to scold the people for their bad behaviour as a result of following that teaching. Therefore he encouraged them to not believe that teaching because they should only believe the teaching concerning the messiah. They also need to be adding the following to their faith: good behaviour, wisdom/knowledge, self-control, patience, obeying God, and loving others.
\ip Those people taught that the messiah would not return since it had already been quite a while and he hadn't yet returned. But Simon answered by saying that the messiah would certainly return, but God doesn't want to punish everyone, but desires that people would turn away from their sins.
\iot Main components of Peter's letter
\io1 Introduction \ior 1:1-2\ior*
\io1 The calling of Christians \ior 1:3-21\ior*
\io1 False teachers \ior 2:1-22\ior*
\io1 The messiah Yeshua's return \ior 3:1-18\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
